---
/**
 * AIGC for Retailers  ·  /solutions/retailers
 *
 * Speed-of-scroll content production for retail. Drawn from the source
 * page's reality-check (speed, scale, market momentum) and the five lanes
 * where AIGC actually changes retail output.
 *
 * Per repo standards: no em-dashes (U+2014), no decorative numerals inside
 * cards or repeated blocks, body copy at var(--type-body), hubStudio keeps
 * its canonical lowercase-h casing.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';

const colourBar = [
  '#e94e1b', '#c73e10', '#1e3a8a', '#0e1f4e', '#0e1633',
  '#6b6b73', '#a8a299', '#d8d3cb', '#e5e1db', '#ffffff',
];

const reasons = [
  {
    label: 'Speed of scroll',
    title: 'In retail, relevance happens at the speed of scroll.',
    body: 'While you brief photographers for next season, competitors are already testing, optimising and converting with AI-generated content tuned to every audience segment. The shooting calendar is no longer the constraint that protects the brand, it is the constraint that costs it the quarter.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Scale reality',
    title: 'Eighty seasonal campaigns, thousands of assets, all live.',
    body: 'Each campaign needs product shots, lifestyle photography, social content and localised market variants. Traditional production: months of coordination, hundreds of thousands in budget and content that is outdated before launch. AIGC delivers the same library at a fraction of the cost.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Market momentum',
    title: 'AIGC adoption is no longer a curve, it is a moat.',
    body: 'Retailers using AI-generated content see 70% faster time-to-market and up to 40% cost reduction while testing ten times more creative. Eighty-four percent of ecommerce businesses now put AI at the top of their priority list. The line between the early adopters and the followers is widening.',
  },
];

const lanes = [
  {
    label: 'Product storytelling',
    heading: 'Product storytelling at infinite scale.',
    image: '/Images/ecom-imagery.jpg',
    alt: 'A daylit product still life on a kitchen counter, late-afternoon window light from camera left, warm shadow grade, generous negative space.',
    lead: 'One 3D scan, infinite contextual lifestyle scenes across seasons, demographics and use cases.',
    body: [
      "A winter coat lives authentically in mountain lodges, city streets and professional settings, each variation speaking to a different segment without an additional shoot. 360-degree product images increase add-to-cart rates by 22%. AIGC ships dozens of variations at a fraction of the traditional cost.",
      'The same starting asset becomes the hero shot, the editorial frame, the in-context lifestyle scene and the marketplace tile, all tracked against the same brand standard rather than rebuilt every time the campaign moves channel.',
    ],
    tags: [
      '3D-scan starting assets', '360-degree views',
      'Lifestyle contexts', 'Demographic variants',
      'Seasonal extensions', 'Hero / tile / detail',
      'Brand-standard QC',
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'Seasonal agility',
    heading: 'Seasonal agility that outpaces the trend cycle.',
    image: '/Images/pmd-factory.jpg',
    alt: 'A documentary in-studio frame of a retail content team reviewing seasonal creative on a large monitor, warm window light, lifted black point.',
    lead: 'Launch Black Friday campaigns that adapt in real time. Test hundreds of approaches while competitors wait on availability.',
    body: [
      'Generate culturally authentic Valentine campaigns across markets in the time it used to take to confirm the brief. During Black Friday 2024, retailers using AI saw 15% conversion lift through seasonal responsiveness alone.',
      'Useful where the season is short and the variants are many: holiday windows, regional moments, sales events, partner-led pushes. The same hero idea ships in twenty contexts before the photographer would have finished one.',
    ],
    tags: [
      'Real-time adaptation', 'Multi-market variants',
      'Concept testing at scale', 'Seasonal hero refresh',
      'Holiday-window creative', 'Partner co-brand variants',
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'Commerce assets',
    heading: 'Commerce assets that convert.',
    image: '/Images/ecom-listings.jpg',
    alt: 'A clean marketplace product layout on a calibrated monitor, with tile, hero and lifestyle variants pinned in a contact-sheet grid alongside.',
    lead: 'Every product deserves hero treatment, every listing deserves a context that lets the shopper see themselves in the product.',
    body: [
      'Generate pristine product photography, 360-degree views and demonstration videos that lead with the features customers actually care about. Lifestyle contexts help shoppers envision the product in their lives. 67% of consumers describe image quality as "very important" to the purchase decision.',
      'AIGC fills the bottom of the funnel as well as the top: PDP heroes, A+ content, configurator stills, comparison tables, returns-prevention angle shots. The library that closes the sale, rebuilt at the pace the calendar actually moves.',
    ],
    tags: [
      'PDP hero photography', '360-degree views',
      'Demonstration video', 'Lifestyle contexts',
      'A+ content', 'Comparison frames',
      'Returns-prevention shots',
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'Social commerce',
    heading: 'Hyper-relevant social commerce.',
    image: '/Images/sb-sample-branded.jpg',
    alt: 'A social-first video frame of a model holding a product, vertical aspect, soft natural daylight, prime-lens shallow focus.',
    lead: 'Social content that performs across platforms, audiences and cultural contexts, each variation crafted for the moment.',
    body: [
      'A sustainable fashion line gets one creative treatment for Gen Z advocates, another for millennial professionals, same product, infinite relevant expressions. Social commerce revenue is on track to reach $6.2 trillion by 2030; the brands that capture it ship at the pace the platform demands.',
      'Useful where the channel mix is wide, the formats are fast and the appetite for new creative is constant. AIGC industrialises the variation layer so the team can spend its energy on the next idea rather than the next render.',
    ],
    tags: [
      'Platform-specific cuts', 'Audience-specific variants',
      'UGC-style adaptations', 'Vertical / square / wide',
      'Caption-aware framing', 'Trend-led concept tests',
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'Global consistency',
    heading: 'Global consistency, local authenticity.',
    image: '/Images/md-ooh.jpg',
    alt: 'An out-of-home campaign frame on a city wall at the end of the afternoon, single low-angle sun source, warm shadow grade, restrained composition.',
    lead: 'Maintain brand integrity while speaking native languages of emotion and culture.',
    body: [
      "Beauty products look naturally at home in Scandinavian minimalism or vibrant African patterns, each expressing authentic cultural relevance without losing the brand line. AI absorbs the localisation labour so the brand standard is the only thing the team has to police.",
      'Useful for any retailer running more than one market: campaign launches, partnership variants, seasonal pushes, sale events. The hero idea travels intact; the cultural surface adapts.',
    ],
    tags: [
      'Cultural adaptation', 'Native-market variants',
      'Brand-standard QC', 'Localised props',
      'Region-specific casting', 'Language-aware frames',
    ],
  },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How quickly can we generate content for seasonal campaigns?',
    a: 'Complete seasonal campaigns in days, not months. From a single product scan, we create hundreds of lifestyle variations across contexts and demographics. Launch marketing six to eight weeks earlier than traditional workflows. Fast-moving clients go from concept to market-ready assets in 72 hours.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can AI-generated content maintain our brand consistency across global markets?',
    a: 'Yes. We establish the brand visual DNA (colour, styling, composition) then apply it consistently across every generated piece. The products keep their brand expression while adapting to local cultural contexts, from Scandinavian minimalism to vibrant African patterns.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does AIGC handle complex product categories like fashion or technical products?',
    a: 'Fashion gets lifestyle contexts showing fit and styling across body types. Technical products get detailed feature callouts and demonstration scenarios. The AI adapts to each category: lifestyle visualisation for apparel, functionality highlights for tech.',
  },
  {
    q: "What's the cost comparison between AIGC and traditional product photography?",
    a: 'Up to 40% cost reduction while doubling creative output. Traditional shoots cost $50,000 to $200,000 for a seasonal campaign. AIGC generates equivalent volume at a fraction of that, with budget flexibility for dozens of variations after the initial setup.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do we ensure product accuracy in AI-generated images?',
    a: 'We start with high-resolution 3D scans capturing exact dimensions, textures and colour. Quality control runs verification checklists for product detail and brand compliance. AI maintains photographic consistency better than traditional shoots, so accurate expectations on the PDP mean lower return rates.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can AIGC adapt content in real time based on performance data?',
    a: 'Yes. Data-driven optimisation analyses conversion, engagement and performance metrics, then refines the approach. If lifestyle contexts outperform product shots, we generate more lifestyle variations. The content evolves based on actual shopper behaviour.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does platform optimisation work across different channels?',
    a: 'AI generates optimised versions from a single source asset. Instagram gets vibrant lifestyle, Amazon gets clean product with callouts, TikTok gets dynamic youth context. The same product speaks fluent platform languages simultaneously, without a separate creative brief per channel.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What kind of conversion-rate improvements can we expect?',
    a: 'Significant performance lift: 15 to 30% from AI-optimised images, 27% higher conversion with enhanced visual experience, 4.5% lift with user-generated content integration. Strategic visual upgrades have driven conversion improvements above 25% for some clients.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do we integrate AIGC with our existing content workflow?',
    a: 'A hybrid approach. The studio enhances your creative teams rather than replacing them. Brand managers provide direction, AI generates variations at scale, teams select final assets. We work inside your CMS or DAM and respect the approval chain.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens if we need traditional photography for certain campaigns?',
    a: 'The hybrid model includes real studio execution when needed. Luxury products, hero moments and celebrity collaborations still benefit from traditional photography. Real shoots combine with AIGC enhancement, extending the hero across contexts and demographics, so the campaign keeps the authenticity and gains the scale.',
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};
---

<Layout
  title="AIGC for Retailers | Scale Visual Assets, Boost Conversions | hubStudio"
  description="AI-generated content for retail marketing: unlimited product variations, seasonal campaigns, faster launches and conversion-grade visuals across every channel."
>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <div class="prog" aria-hidden="true"><span class="prog__bar"></span></div>

  <div class="page">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero__panel">
        <svg class="hero__reg" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
          <path d="M50 4v92M4 50h92" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
        </svg>
        <div class="hero__panel-in">
          <p class="kicker kicker--light r">
            <span class="kicker__tick"></span>Solutions
            <span class="kicker__sep">/</span> Retailers
          </p>
          <h1 class="hero__title">
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i">Transform the</span></span>
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i">retail content</span></span>
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i serif">game.</span></span>
          </h1>
          <p class="hero__tag r" style="--d:.45s">
            Every product, every touchpoint, every market, <em>without breaking the calendar</em>.
          </p>
          <div class="hero__lead r" style="--d:.55s">
            <p>
              The retail content problem is no longer about ideas. It is
              about volume, speed and the cultural fit of every asset that
              hits a tile or a feed. Traditional production cannot keep up.
              The brands that adapt first compound the advantage.
            </p>
            <p>
              We architect retail content systems that ship thousands of
              brand-correct assets a month, across categories and markets,
              tracked against the same creative standard the studio holds
              itself to.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hero__cta r" style="--d:.65s">
            <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Start a retail brief</Button>
            <a class="ghost-link ghost-link--light" href="#lanes">
              See the lanes
              <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M4 10h12M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero__meta r" style="--d:.72s">
            Shanghai studio <span>/</span> 35+ markets, marketplace-ready assets
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__visual">
        <img
          src="/Images/retailers-hero.jpg"
          alt="A retail product still life on a sunlit kitchen counter with late-afternoon window light from camera left, prime-lens shallow focus, warm shadow grade and generous negative space."
          width="1024"
          height="1024"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
        <span class="hero__chip">Shanghai <span>/</span> Retail floor</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="cbar" aria-hidden="true">
      {colourBar.map((c) => <span style={`background:${c}`}></span>)}
    </div>

    <section class="why">
      <div class="shell">
        <header class="band band--split">
          <div>
            <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Reality check</p>
            <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
              The retail content reality<br />has <span class="serif">already shifted</span>.
            </h2>
          </div>
          <p class="band__note band__note--light r" style="--d:.1s">
            Three forces define the new floor: the pace of the scroll, the
            volume the calendar demands and the moat that early AIGC
            adopters are quietly compounding. The brands waiting for the
            next pitch are paying for the gap.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="reasons">
          {
            reasons.map((r, i) => (
              <article class="reason r" style={`--d:${i * 0.08}s`}>
                <p class="reason__label">
                  <span class="reason__tick"></span>
                  {r.label}
                </p>
                <h3 class="reason__title">{r.title}</h3>
                <p class="reason__body">{r.body}</p>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cover" id="lanes">
      <div class="shell">
        <header class="band">
          <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Where AIGC transforms retail</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            Five lanes, one <span class="serif">content engine</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="band__note r" style="--d:.1s">
            Each lane attacks a different retail constraint. Most retailers
            start with product storytelling or commerce assets, then expand
            into seasonal, social and global as the engine proves itself.
          </p>
        </header>

        {
          lanes.map((c, i) => (
            <article class={`feature ${i % 2 === 1 ? 'feature--rev' : ''}`}>
              <figure class="feature__media crop r-clip">
                <div class="crop__inner">
                  <img
                    src={c.image}
                    alt={c.alt}
                    width="1024"
                    height="820"
                    loading="lazy"
                  />
                </div>
                <figcaption class="fig">{c.label}</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <div class="feature__body">
                <p class="feature__idx r">
                  <span class="feature__tick"></span>
                  Retail lane
                </p>
                <h3 class="dh dh--sm r" style="--d:.05s">{c.heading}</h3>
                {c.lead && <p class="feature__lead r" style="--d:.1s">{c.lead}</p>}
                {c.body.map((para, pi) => (
                  <p class="feature__p r" style={`--d:${0.12 + pi * 0.06}s`}>
                    {para}
                  </p>
                ))}
                <p class="feature__scope r" style="--d:.24s">In scope</p>
                <ul class="chips r" style="--d:.28s">
                  {c.tags.map((t) => (
                    <li class="chip">{t}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="source">
      <div class="shell source__grid">
        <div class="source__visual">
          <figure class="source__main crop">
            <div class="crop__inner">
              <img
                src="/Images/who-we-are-china-speed.jpg"
                alt="A documentary frame of hubStudio operators reviewing retail variations on a wall of pinned proofs, warm shadow grade, calibrated stations behind."
                width="1024"
                height="820"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
          </figure>
          <div class="source__stat">
            <span class="source__stat-num">Up to 40%</span>
            <span class="source__stat-cap">Production cost reduction while doubling creative output</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="source__body">
          <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Why hubStudio</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            Results retail leaders<br />actually <span class="serif">recognise</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="source__lead r" style="--d:.1s">
            Three times faster seasonal launches with complete cross-channel
            asset libraries. Twenty-seven percent higher conversion on
            products with enhanced visual experiences. Cost cuts that fund
            the next round of testing rather than the next round of cuts.
          </p>
          <p class="source__p r" style="--d:.16s">
            The methodology is proven inside an active retail studio first,
            then handed to clients. AI implementation lands without
            disrupting the creative culture it joins, because the people
            running it have shipped both sides of the table.
          </p>
          <p class="source__p r" style="--d:.22s">
            That positions the operation at the front of rapidly evolving
            AI capability while building a retail content engine that
            survives the next platform shift rather than being rebuilt by it.
          </p>
          <ul class="creds r" style="--d:.28s">
            <li class="cred">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M2 7.5 5.5 11 12 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
              3x faster launches
            </li>
            <li class="cred">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M2 7.5 5.5 11 12 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
              27% higher CVR
            </li>
            <li class="cred">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M2 7.5 5.5 11 12 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
              Up to 40% cost cut
            </li>
            <li class="cred">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M2 7.5 5.5 11 12 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
              Marketplace-ready
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq">
      <div class="shell faq__grid">
        <aside class="faq__intro">
          <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Questions</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            Before the<br />first <span class="serif">launch</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="faq__sub r" style="--d:.1s">
            The questions retail teams ask before we begin. If yours is not
            below, put it in the brief.
          </p>
          <div class="r" style="--d:.16s">
            <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Start a retail brief</Button>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <div class="acc">
          {
            faqs.map((faq) => (
              <div class="acc__row r">
                <button class="acc__q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                  <span class="acc__qmark">Q</span>
                  <span class="acc__qtext">{faq.q}</span>
                  <span class="acc__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span></span><span></span>
                  </span>
                </button>
                <div class="acc__a">
                  <div class="acc__a-inner">
                    <p>{faq.a}</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="end">
      <svg class="end__reg" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
        <path d="M50 4v92M4 50h92" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
      </svg>
      <div class="shell end__inner">
        <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Build with us</p>
        <h2 class="end__title r" style="--d:.05s">
          Ship retail at<br /><span class="serif">our pace</span>.
        </h2>
        <p class="end__p r" style="--d:.12s">
          Send a category list, a current calendar or just the launch you
          want to move next quarter. A senior lead reads it inside two
          working days and replies with a phased plan, a cost shape and an
          honest read on which lane starts first.
        </p>
        <div class="end__cta r" style="--d:.18s">
          <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Start a retail brief</Button>
          <a class="ghost-link ghost-link--light" href="/work">
            See client work
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M4 10h12M11 5l5 5-5 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cbar cbar--end" aria-hidden="true">
        {colourBar.map((c) => <span style={`background:${c}`}></span>)}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page { --ink: #0e1633; --navy: #0e1f4e; --paper: #f0ede9; --paper-2: #e7e3dd; overflow: clip; }
  .shell { width: 100%; max-width: 1280px; margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: clamp(22px, 5vw, 60px); }
  .prog { position: fixed; inset: 0 0 auto 0; height: 3px; z-index: 200; pointer-events: none; }
  .prog__bar { display: block; height: 100%; width: 100%; transform: scaleX(0); transform-origin: 0 50%; background: var(--brand-orange); }
  .r, .r-clip { --d: 0s; }
  .r { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(26px); transition: opacity 0.7s ease, transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d); }
  .r.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  .r-clip .crop__inner { clip-path: inset(0 0 101% 0); transition: clip-path 1.05s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .r-clip .crop__inner img { transform: scale(1.12); transition: transform 1.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .r-clip.in .crop__inner { clip-path: inset(0 0 0 0); }
  .r-clip.in .crop__inner img { transform: scale(1); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .r, .r.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; }
    .r-clip .crop__inner, .r-clip .crop__inner img { clip-path: none; transform: none; transition: none; }
  }
  .kicker { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .kicker--light { color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.66); }
  .kicker__tick { width: 22px; height: 0; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .kicker__sep { color: var(--brand-orange); }
  .dh { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(34px, 4.4vw, 62px); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .dh--sm { font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 38px); }
  .serif { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-style: italic; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--brand-orange); }
  .crop { position: relative; margin: 0; }
  .crop::before, .crop::after { content: ''; position: absolute; width: 16px; height: 16px; z-index: 2; }
  .crop::before { top: -9px; left: -9px; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); border-left: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .crop::after { right: -9px; bottom: 28px; border-right: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .crop__inner { overflow: hidden; border-radius: 4px; }
  .crop__inner img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .fig { margin-top: 14px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .ghost-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; font-size: var(--type-small); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-ink); }
  .ghost-link svg { width: 19px; height: 19px; transition: transform 0.24s ease-out; }
  .ghost-link:hover svg { transform: translateX(5px); }
  .ghost-link--light { color: var(--text-on-dark); }
  .band { max-width: 720px; margin-bottom: clamp(40px, 5vw, 70px); display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .band--split { max-width: none; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 880px) {
    .band--split { grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.82fr; align-items: end; gap: 18px 60px; }
    .band--split > div { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  }
